    seoTitle: 'Partly at Fault in a California Accident | Comparative Fault',
    description: 'How California comparative fault can reduce—rather than automatically eliminate—an injury recovery, and what evidence matters when responsibility is disputed.',
    directAnswer: 'Potentially. California uses comparative-fault principles. CACI 405 instructs that if a defendant proves the plaintiff’s negligence contributed to the harm, damages are reduced by the percentage of responsibility assigned to the plaintiff. The actual allocation depends on the evidence and legal duties of everyone involved.',
